==Battleground==
*3 [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]] spawns.
*2 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 30~50 seconds<sup>900f~1,500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doge Dark]] (10%) spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
**16 [[Doge Dark]]s (400%) spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
**6 [[Gary Gory|Gary Gories]] spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**2 [[Teacher A]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
As the Teacher A. don't outrange [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|C. Bahamut]], the real threat are the Gory Garies, who, on half health, deal 9k a hit, being able to tear through tanky units, and are a general nuisance, especially with the Shadow Boxer Ks. This basically means you're gonna need to bring out the cheap spammable meatshields to protect your Bahamut. [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] is quite helpful as well to deal with the Gary Gories.

==Trivia==
*The stage name is a reference to the [[wikipedia:Haber process|Haber Process]].

